wc - count newlines, words and bytes

SYNOPSIS
    wc [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    For each file, print the newline count, word count, byte count and
    pathname. With no operands, count standard input and omit the pathname.
    Words are runs of bytes separated by whitespace.

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), grep(1)
